\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Caller's decision threshold $c(L)$. At hand strength of exactly $c(L)$, the caller is indifferent between calling and folding. Since the value of calling weakly increases with $y$, it must be weakly greater than 0 for $y > c(L)$ and weakly less than 0 for $y < c(L)$. Folding always has value 0.\relax }}{36}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:caller_threshold}{{9}{36}{Caller's decision threshold $c(L)$. At hand strength of exactly $c(L)$, the caller is indifferent between calling and folding. Since the value of calling weakly increases with $y$, it must be weakly greater than 0 for $y > c(L)$ and weakly less than 0 for $y < c(L)$. Folding always has value 0.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
